module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.gate_reported_success_on_a_phase_it_refused

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data gate_reported_success_on_a_phase_it_refused: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "gate_reported_success_on_a_phase_it_refused" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**a required lane printed a typed, located refusal for a phase it ran, counted it, and then exited 0, so the job, the aggregating required context and the pull request all reported green while a required observation had been DECLINED** (INVALID STATE: the refusal arm is correct and reaches the log in full -- `required-ci: floor refused: REQUIRED-FLOOR REFUSAL cause=...`, `phases_failed=1`, `required-ci: FAILED PHASE ...` -- and the process still returns SUCCESS. Nothing is silent except the one thing that decides: the exit status. This is DESIGN section 5's forbidden arm inside the gate itself, and section 4b(1) rung inflation at the gate's own grain: the lane reported the rung its clean run would have established for a run that did not hold.",

    "SPECIMEN, TWO INDEPENDENT RUNS, verified against the GitHub jobs API and not only from the step log. Run 35503853026 (head cb39f95 of session/still-lynx-398), floor job 106060214538: the log carries `required-ci: floor refused: REQUIRED-FLOOR REFUSAL cause=ChangedWitnessObservationFailed ... the base side could not be reconstructed (dag/std/types.dag differs ...)`, then `required-ci: lane=witnesses phases_run=2 phases_failed=1`, then `required-ci: FAILED PHASE floor refused: ...`, and the step carrying it concluded SUCCESS, as did the job. Run 35510547600 (head e78927a), floor job 106077573881: the same shape and the same cause.",

    "THE MECHANISM, derived from the chain and not from the symptom link. `claim_executor --required-ci` maps phase outcomes to an exit in two places. Without `--measurement-receipt` it refuses correctly on a non-empty phase-failure set. WITH the flag it wrote the receipt and returned SUCCESS unconditionally, because the D0 design it was written for published the receipt and let a SEPARATE step adjudicate it: measure with `continue-on-error`, upload, then `--adjudicate-measurement-receipt`. That split was real and it was correct. gunbc#11742 (2026-09-19) moved the emission of `.github/workflows/witnesses.yml` from `gunbc.witness_floor_workflow` to `gunbc.compiler_gate_workflow`, and that emission carried NO receipt command at all -- checked, not assumed: `--measurement-receipt` appears zero times in the YAML at 85c1356300c. gunbc#11791 (2026-09-20 05:18 UTC) then restored a floor job by copying the witness floor's receipt-BEARING command into a lane that has no adjudicating step and no `continue-on-error` -- deliberately, as `compiler_gate_floor_run_step`'s own note says, `here a refused claim refuses the lane`. The measuring process became the only authority left standing on a route where it had been built to decide nothing.",

    "SO THE EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY IS THE FLAG'S CONTRACT, NOT THE CONSUMER. `--measurement-receipt` conflated two facts: WRITE A RECEIPT and DO NOT DECIDE. A consumer that wants the first without the second could not ask for it, and the one that arrived got the second by silence. The repair is at that boundary: the measuring process now adjudicates the FILE it just wrote and returns that verdict, through the same function the separate adjudicating mode uses. Restoring the split costs nothing -- a step carrying `continue-on-error` absorbs the status and its adjudicator reads the same receipt to the same verdict.",

    "A SECOND LEAK IN THE SAME BRANCH, found by the audit the first one forced and closed with it -- and its own repair then introduced a third, narrower one, recorded in the recognition rule below rather than hidden. The blocker set the receipt carries was synthesized from the phase-failure list by comparing a blocker's PHASE to the whole failure SENTENCE, and by exempting the failure spelled exactly `floor`. So a floor that reported not-clean while yielding no blockers of its own produced a COMPLETED measurement with an EMPTY blocker set -- a failed phase with nothing to adjudicate, which the repaired exit would have read as clean. The comparison is now phase word against phase word and no phase is exempt.",

    "WHAT THE REFUSAL ITSELF IS, held apart so no future reader repairs the wrong half. When a changed kernel file such as `dag/std/types.dag` makes the base side impossible to reconstruct, the changed-witness sublane DECLINES TO PLAN rather than widening to the whole corpus or narrowing to nothing. That is DESIGN section 5's absorbing-fallback rule obeyed exactly, and it stays. What was wrong was only the exit status and what the pull request view was told.",

    "BOUNDED AGAINST THE NEIGHBOURS. It is not `downstream_upload_failure_read_as_adjudication_cause`: there the adjudicator RAN and refused and the reader mis-attributed the cause; here no adjudicator ran at all. It is not `command_not_found_exit_cannot_distinguish_eviction_from_misnaming`: the process returned normally and chose SUCCESS. It is not `measure_mode_command_emitted_into_a_lane_with_no_adjudicator`, filed by gunbc#11836 for the same incident and deliberately kept beside this row rather than merged into it: that class is about an EMISSION -- a lane command copied into a workflow whose job roster cannot discharge it -- and its wall is at the emitter, which refuses to render such a lane. This class is about what the INSTRUMENT returns when it is asked to measure and nothing adjudicates: the two are the same night's receipt read from the two ends, and closing either one leaves the other's arm live. It is not a defect in `v2.workflow.required_ci_measurement`, whose model was right the whole time -- `required_ci_measurement_admitted` admits a measurement exactly when it completed with no blockers, and `v2.test.required_ci_measurement` has witnessed both arms since it landed. A correct model with a realization that never consulted it is the conformance-realization row of DESIGN section 3b, not a modeling gap.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, and it generalizes past this lane: for any gate, ask what its FAILURE ARM RETURNS, not what it PRINTS. A counted, typed, located diagnostic beside a zero exit is the shape. The mechanical tell is a success return inside a branch that is also the branch which writes evidence -- publication and verdict fused in a reader's mind and separated in the code. The audit that goes with the rule: enumerate every arm that appends to the failure set and confirm each one reaches the exit; on the repaired lane there are twenty-two appends to that set and every one of them reaches the exit. THE RECEIPT IS A SECOND OBLIGATION AND THE FIRST REPAIR FAILED IT, which is recorded here because it is the same class one layer in: the fix for the empty-blocker-set leak deduped the published blockers BY PHASE WORD, and the phase words are not unique -- `generated-artifact` carries six distinct failure sentences and `regen-fixed-point` four -- so every cause after the first in each phase was dropped from the receipt the separate adjudicating consumer reads. The exit stayed non-zero throughout, which is precisely why nothing caught it: the status was right while the located diagnostic was gone. Found in review 69681 and repaired by deduping on the CAUSE, with a bare phase word treated as a summary that publishes only when its phase minted no blockers of its own.",

    "CONSEQUENCE, BOUNDED BY WHAT THE HISTORY SUPPORTS. The blind window opens at gunbc#11791 (merged 2026-09-20 05:18 UTC), the commit that put a receipt-bearing lane command into a job with no adjudicator, and closes when the lane stops reporting success over blockers. Within it, any required run whose floor phase refused -- most reachably a pull request touching a file the base reconstruction needs, such as `dag/std/types.dag` -- reported green with its changed-witness observation never made. Two such runs are named above as verified receipts. The claim is NOT that it reaches further back, and an earlier draft of this row said #11742 on the reasoning that the adjudicator left there; that is wrong and the correction is kept rather than quietly replaced, because the discriminator is cheap and was available: the flag appears ZERO times in the YAML emitted at 85c1356300c. Before #11791 there was no receipt command in this workflow to be unadjudicated, and before #11742 the published receipt was adjudicated by its own step.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The refusal was total, typed and located; only the status lied, and it lied in the direction the ladder forbids.",

    "RUNG NOW: mechanically preventable, and the honesty bound is stated rather than implied. The admission relation and its readback are in `v1_compiler.cli_run.required_ci_measurement` with a discriminating red (a completed measurement carrying one blocker must never be admitted, executed through the write and the readback, not asserted against a string) and its green control. Those controls execute on `cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib`, which `gunbc.rung_drop` `rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path` declares is run by NO CI step -- so the enrolled-and-executing half of the rung is local diligence, and what runs on the merge path is the green arm only, once per required run, by the lane itself.",

    "CEILING: structurally impossible, and it is reachable rather than aspirational. The invalid state is a process exit that disagrees with an admission verdict, and it has no constructor once the exit is DERIVED from the verdict instead of chosen beside it -- which is what the v2 CLI's `std.process` `ProcessExit` value already makes possible for a lane whose decision is a fold.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, A CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT: the required lane's phase-outcome-to-exit decision evaluated as a `.dag` fold returning `std.process` `ProcessExit`, with the seed's `main` performing only the status set -- SUFFICIENT FOR a lane that cannot express a success exit over a non-empty blocker set, so that neither this arm nor a future one can choose a status the verdict does not carry. `v2.cli.compile_cli` is the existing instance of that shape; the required lane is not yet on it.)",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.required_ci_measurement", decl_name: "required_ci_measurement_admitted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_ci_measurement", decl_name: "adjudicate_required_ci_measurement", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_ci_measurement", decl_name: "adjudicate_required_ci_measurement_receipt_file", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.compiler_gate_workflow", decl_name: "compiler_gate_floor_run_step", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.witness_floor_workflow", decl_name: "required_ci_measurement_adjudicate_step", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
